  "summary": "Project manager, team lead, consultant, and developer on projects that have included application and system requirements gathering, application maintenance and support, web-related programming, GUI design, information architecture, technical writing, and content management experience. \n\n• Technical Project Manager: Develop strategies and solutions to implement complex projects and overcome technical obstacles.  Manage teams to deliver projects on time, and within scope and budget.\n\n• Release Manager: Coordinate and manage large project teams to ensure project milestones are met, and develop deployment plans and instructions.  Manage release activities and communicate to customer and management teams on project status.\n\n• Infrastructure SME: Provide support and lead issues to resolution across IBM’s Procurement production infrastructure.  Manage changes across servers and applications ensuring audit preparedness and compliance.\n\n• Internet Development: Coordinate and lead team, design, develop, and test application in agile iterations for internal IBM and commercial customer in consumer goods, government, medical, and manufacturing industries.\n\n• Web Architect: Work with customers to create design specifications and implementation strategies based on software and hardware requirements.  Update and maintain system architecture documentation for IBM Procurement infrastructure.\n\n• Interface Design & Usability: Develop application prototypes and present designs to external customers.  Create use cases for internal and external clients and run scenarios with end users to gather feedback on refining and improving the user experience for web applications.\n\n• Content and Information Design: Organize, structure and label content effectively for internal and external customers using a wide array of content management tools.\n\n• Technical Writing: Work directly with development teams to create installation instructions that are used for software and application upgrades.",
